{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1032752-awakened-house-and-stats","id":1032752,"title":"Awakened house and stats","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-16T10:20:28-08:00","id":1032752,"title":"Awakened house and stats","content":"Would an awakened house have stats, incase it ever had to defend against an intruder? I'm not entirely sure how it'd work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T10:28:33-08:00","id":1032755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingJohn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1032752-awakened-house-and-stats#post1032752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would an awakened house have stats, incase it ever had to defend against an intruder? I'm not entirely sure how it'd work.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think more details would be needed to give a proper answer. Specifically answers about the house itself. A brand new home (built in the last 10-20 years) probably wouldn't have much of a spirit to awaken, whereas something old with a lot of history would have an awakened spirit with some gusto behind it. But in neither case is it a given fact that the spirit in question will have the power to do much against intruders. It might, it might not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T10:43:39-08:00","id":1032765,"title":"","content":"The level of power of the spirit as Vysha said would depend a lot on its age. The charms however would be similar. I'm not familiar enough withall the charms to just rattle them off but the house should be able to have control over everything fixed to the house, doors windows and such. It should also be a bit more resistant to damage though it could certainly still be destroyed. Other offensive charms would need to be decided by the ST but outright destructive charms would be doubtful. When manifesting physically it would probably be quite large and slow with many health levels and moderately high strength. Again this is ultimately up to the ST.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T13:59:52-08:00","id":1032897,"title":"","content":"I'm going to assume it would not need the materialize charm to do things in the skinlands. (I.E., lock out intruders, attack them with the house, etc)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T16:51:00-08:00","id":1032999,"title":"","content":"I'd say that watching <i>The Haunting </i>(1963 version, avoid the remake) might provide some fertile ground for inspiration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T17:25:41-08:00","id":1033029,"title":"","content":"It's probably going to need Reach. Is it going to be possessing the house (there's a Charm for possessing the inanimate). <br /> <br /> If it does have Materialize, then there's some issues about WHAT would Materialize? I mean the house is already there, right? So if it does Materialize it's going to be the spirit of the house in the house.... <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T18:00:10-08:00","id":1033063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1032752-awakened-house-and-stats?p=1033029#post1033029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's probably going to need Reach. Is it going to be possessing the house (there's a Charm for possessing the inanimate).<br /> <br /> If it does have Materialize, then there's some issues about WHAT would Materialize? I mean the house is already there, right? So if it does Materialize it's going to be the spirit of the house in the house....<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It is the house-.....So why would the house possess it's functions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T18:40:32-08:00","id":1033083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1032752-awakened-house-and-stats?p=1033029#post1033029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it does have Materialize, then there's some issues about WHAT would Materialize?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://s-media-cache-ak0.pinimg.com/originals/62/18/9e/62189e21a62c6edc11a6a4d22ec6c14e.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Probably something like this</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T21:06:08-08:00","id":1033131,"title":"","content":"The house of Baba Yaga, cool (the russian folklore myth, not the 4th generation Vampire).<br /> <br /> The spirit of the house wouldn't &quot;posses&quot; the house, it IS the house, only with it's spirit awakened. Possess the inanime is for ANOTHER spirit to possess some inanimate objetc; so, it would be needed for an fire elemental to make an marble statue to move, but if you awake the spirit of that statue, that spirit is not &quot;possessing&quot; it, no more than your Avatar &quot;possess&quot; YOU. Now, if I use Spirit 5 (or would it be 4?) to rip away the spirit of my statue, the material statue will crumble to dust if I break it's silver cord, and I can trap the statue's spirit into another object.<br /> <br /> But I can also try to make an spiritual cat, for example, try to possess my statue with the awaken spirit... That would be akin to a wraith trying to posses a living person, and both spirits probably would fight with their will for control.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T21:10:38-08:00","id":1033133,"title":"","content":"And a awakened spirit cannot materialize because... Well... It's already in this plane. It IS the house, not an alien telekitic making ghosts pranks. That would be like asking for an Avatar to materialize... It is already material, in the form of the Mage (or sleeper)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T05:46:55-08:00","id":1033287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1032752-awakened-house-and-stats?p=1033131#post1033131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The house of Baba Yaga, cool (the russian folklore myth, not the 4th generation Vampire).<br /> <br /> The spirit of the house wouldn't &amp;quot;posses&amp;quot; the house, it IS the house, only with it's spirit awakened. Possess the inanime is for ANOTHER spirit to possess some inanimate objetc; so, it would be needed for an fire elemental to make an marble statue to move, but if you awake the spirit of that statue, that spirit is not &amp;quot;possessing&amp;quot; it, no more than your Avatar &amp;quot;possess&amp;quot; YOU. Now, if I use Spirit 5 (or would it be 4?) to rip away the spirit of my statue, the material statue will crumble to dust if I break it's silver cord, and I can trap the statue's spirit into another object.<br /> <br /> But I can also try to make an spiritual cat, for example, try to possess my statue with the awaken spirit... That would be akin to a wraith trying to posses a living person, and both spirits probably would fight with their will for control.</div> </div> </div> </div>So it wouldn't need charms then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T05:58:25-08:00","id":1033291,"title":"","content":"So it could have charms in addition to its control of the house's functions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T07:13:35-08:00","id":1033339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingJohn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1032752-awakened-house-and-stats?p=1033291#post1033291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it could have charms in addition to its control of the house's functions?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, though the extent of the spirits control over its material correspondence (in this case, the house) without using Charms is left up to the ST. The bulk of this conversation is unfortunately ST fiat. We've only ever been given vague generalities on awakened spirits and what they can actually do (or even the extent of their newly awakened sentience).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T09:25:40-08:00","id":1033403,"title":"","content":"Just as an idea, here's what I as an ST would rule an awakened house with a good level of self awareness to be capable of doing:<br /> <br /> Slamming and locking doors<br /> Having the windows open just enough to let the wind whistle.<br /> Increase or decrease the temperature via thermostat<br /> Allow segments of wall or ceiling to crumble away.<br /> Flicker lights or cut the power all together.<br /> Create all kinds of noises from creaking to sudden thumps (great for misleading pursuers)<br /> allow or deny entry into hidden crawlspaces.<br /> start fires (not something a house would do without a really good reason, as it means almost certain destruction)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 01-17-2017, 01:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T13:13:05-08:00","id":1033583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1032752-awakened-house-and-stats?p=1033403#post1033403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just as an idea, here's what I as an ST would rule an awakened house with a good level of self awareness to be capable of doing:<br /> <br /> Slamming and locking doors<br /> Having the windows open just enough to let the wind whistle.<br /> Increase or decrease the temperature via thermostat<br /> Allow segments of wall or ceiling to crumble away.<br /> Flicker lights or cut the power all together.<br /> Create all kinds of noises from creaking to sudden thumps (great for misleading pursuers)<br /> allow or deny entry into hidden crawlspaces.<br /> start fires (not something a house would do without a really good reason, as it means almost certain destruction)</div> </div> </div> </div>That's basically it. I would let it do anything a human in the real world could do inside a house. Slam door, turn any machine on or off, turning the gas, and so on. It might be a good idea to make some mundane changes in your &quot;magical haunted house&quot; to make it more... Lets say... &quot;Effective&quot;. Like, for example, placing an automatic machine gun controlled with electricity in the entrance hall. Oh, your house-buddy would love that toy!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T13:19:11-08:00","id":1033588,"title":"","content":"Wanna make a pit bellow your living house with a trap door with sharks on it? Sure buddy! Deadly lasers in your living room? Hell, why not! An electrical dimensional portal that summons banes in your room? Go for it!<br /> <br /> Just make sure to never piss your house... And keep it very clean... ALWAYS!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T13:34:06-08:00","id":1033604,"title":"","content":"Now I'm imagining this house getting fed up by how dirty it's owner has left it, so it starts turning on the television to cleaning product infomercials and keeps closet doors open with vacuum cleaners inside just to get their point across. And if that doesn't work, then the house just resorts to locking them in until they clean everything up to a good standard.<br /> <br /> &quot;Jim, Why were you late to work?<br /> &quot;I forgot to clean my house.&quot;<br /> &quot;There's plenty of time to clean it after work.&quot;<br /> &quot;Tell that to my house.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T13:41:15-08:00","id":1033609,"title":"","content":"If your house, or part of it are the sanctum of you, then you have arguably a stronger Spirit.<br /> Inside your Sanctum your Paradigm holds sway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T13:58:58-08:00","id":1033620,"title":"","content":"If it got too annoying you could always threaten to hire Hildy from <i>Trading Spaces</i> to redecorate. Sure that would frighten it back into behaving...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T15:14:39-08:00","id":1033678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vysha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1032752-awakened-house-and-stats?p=1033083#post1033083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://s-media-cache-ak0.pinimg.com/originals/62/18/9e/62189e21a62c6edc11a6a4d22ec6c14e.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Probably something like this</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, that's not a House spirit materialized. That's a House with an Awakened Spirit that can use Charms to add crap to the house or morph aspects of the house into crap and then possess the damn thing.<br /> <br /> A House spirit materialized would look like some visualization of the house in some discrete, probably animate form. Like a City Spirit doesn't really look like a skyline, it looks like a person whose traits embody the aspects of the city in question. The spirit of the house might look like a cat, or take on an amalgam of the traits of the housewives who have spent almost every waking hour there for generations or a Transformer version of a Barbie's Playhouse style dollhouse or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T16:03:34-08:00","id":1033704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1032752-awakened-house-and-stats?p=1033678#post1033678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, that's not a House spirit materialized. That's a House with an Awakened Spirit that can use Charms to add crap to the house or morph aspects of the house into crap and then possess the damn thing.<br /> <br /> A House spirit materialized would look like some visualization of the house in some discrete, probably animate form. Like a City Spirit doesn't really look like a skyline, it looks like a person whose traits embody the aspects of the city in question. The spirit of the house might look like a cat, or take on an amalgam of the traits of the housewives who have spent almost every waking hour there for generations or a Transformer version of a Barbie's Playhouse style dollhouse or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the spirit wants to look like Baba Yaga's house, let the spirit look like Baba Yaga's house.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T17:11:19-08:00","id":1033744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1032752-awakened-house-and-stats?p=1033704#post1033704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If the spirit wants to look like Baba Yaga's house, let the spirit look like Baba Yaga's house.</div> </div> </div> </div>It won't BE the house then. It will be the manifested spirit of the house inside the house, outside the house, wherever... and whatever it looks like.<br /> <br /> I can't imange most houses would have somehow gained the self-image of a doorless hut with chicken legs, since, ya know, that's not a thing houses are or do... maybe a mobile home that was ill-used as a chicken coop?<br /> <br /> And, TBH, talking about the house's spirit manifesting doesn't really answer the OP, does it? Since that's not what is being asked. It's about Awakening the house then having it act. It's unlikely that a recently Awakened house is going to have much of a coherent identity as is and it's not entirely relevant what the house's self-image would be if it did have one that wasn't, ya know, IT as it stands in the material world. The question is about what an Awakened house can DO. Which is probably more along the lines of &quot;slam doors&quot; than &quot;turn into giant chicken legged chicken coop&quot; or &quot;appear in the living room as a miniature whirling chicken legged chicken coop&quot;.<br /> <br /> I just had the mages in my game Awaken their car (so it could drive itself around town as a decoy for those nasty Technocrats following them). The car didn't manifest a little mechanical gremlin on the hood for them to talk to. The car started using sampled lyrics, commercials and radio chat to form sentences as &quot;switching the radio station&quot; is something related to the functionality, like houses have doors that open and close. <br /> <br /> An effective Awakened house might try to lure bad guys to the basement and blow up the water heater.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1062,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","user":"Ajax","date":". 01-17-2017, 08:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T17:22:18-08:00","id":1033755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1032752-awakened-house-and-stats?p=1033678#post1033678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, that's not a House spirit materialized.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, <i><b>somebody</b></i> doesn't like fun!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T17:35:49-08:00","id":1033760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vysha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1032752-awakened-house-and-stats?p=1033755#post1033755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, <i><b>somebody</b></i> doesn't like fun!</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. 100% immune to fun.<br /> <br /> Of course, actually attempting to <i>answer </i>the question..... <br /> <br /> No one in my games has ever asked for or expected that if they used Spirit 3 on their House, they would get Baba Yaga's Hut. I'm pretty sure no one would even ask, because they would know that such things are likely to draw attention from those with whom they would not wish to come into conflict....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"